---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Medical Disclaimer"
  description="Naturally Restful publishes health information, not medical advice. Read this before acting on anything we write."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Medical Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="lead">The short version: we inform, your doctor decides. Last updated: September 2026.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>No medical advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on Naturally Restful — articles, comparisons, emails, or comments — is medical
        advice, diagnosis, or treatment. We publish general health <em>information</em> drawn
        from published research. Applying information to your specific situation is a job for a
        qualified healthcare professional who knows your history.
      </p>

      <h2>Supplement statements</h2>
      <p>
        Statements about supplements on this site have not been evaluated by the US Food and
        Drug Administration (FDA) or the European Food Safety Authority (EFSA). No product
        mentioned is intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.
      </p>

      <h2>Before taking any supplement</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Talk to your doctor or pharmacist, especially if you are pregnant, nursing, under 18, or taking any medication.</li>
        <li>Supplements interact with real drugs (e.g., ashwagandha and thyroid medication, melatonin and anticoagulants, magnesium and certain antibiotics).</li>
        <li>"Natural" does not mean safe. Cyanide is natural. Evaluate risk, not vibes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If you have a sleep disorder</h2>
      <p>
        Chronic insomnia, sleep apnea, restless legs, and similar conditions are medical
        conditions with effective medical treatments. No supplement replaces that care. If
        poor sleep is affecting your life, see a doctor first — this site will still be here
        afterward.
      </p>

      <h2>Errors and updates</h2>
      <p>
        Research evolves and we will get things wrong occasionally. We correct publicly with
        updated dates. If you spot an error, <a href="/contact">tell us</a> — corrections are
        handled fastest by email.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
